C2 — Unnecessary Call Overhead


Rule ID
Root cause / pattern
Detection condition
Recommended optimization strategy
Preconditions / constraints
Expected benefit
Supporting reference
C2.S1.R1
Redundant function or method delegation
IF a function only forwards arguments to another function and returns its result without additional logic, THEN flag redundant delegation.
Eliminate redundant delegation: Replace wrapper calls with direct calls to the underlying function.
Preserve validation, side effects, interfaces, and polymorphic behavior.
Reduced function-call overhead and potentially lower execution time and energy consumption.
https://www.usenix.org/conference/java-vm-02/empirical-study-method-lining-java-just-time-compiler

https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/11/3/442
C2.S1.R2
Unnecessary getter/setter or property access
IF a trivial accessor only retrieves or assigns an attribute AND is repeatedly invoked in a hot path, THEN flag unnecessary accessor overhead.
Optimize trivial accessors: Inline getters/setters or replace them with direct attribute access where safe.
Preserve encapsulation, validation, synchronization, and property behavior.
Reduced accessor invocation overhead and faster repeated attribute access.
https://research.tilburguniversity.edu/en/publications/on-the-impact-of-code-smells-on-the-energy-consumption-of-mobile-/



C2.S2.R1
Instance method unnecessarily used for an instance-independent operation
IF a method does not access instance state or require instance-specific behavior, THEN flag it for static conversion.
Convert to static method: Declare the method static instead of using an instance method.
Must not depend on instance state, overriding, or required interface contracts.
Potential reduction in instance-related invocation overhead.
https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/2897073.2897100
C2.S2.R2
Stateless utility operation unnecessarily implemented as an instance method
IF a method performs a general-purpose operation without accessing instance or class state, THEN flag it for extraction.
Extract standalone utility function: Convert the method into a module-level or standalone function.
Preserve dependencies, existing behavior, and API compatibility.
Potential reduction in method-binding overhead and improved code reuse.
https://research.tilburguniversity.edu/en/publications/on-the-impact-of-code-smells-on-the-energy-consumption-of-mobile-/
C2.S3.R1
Excessive invocation of trivial functions in a hot path
IF a frequently executed region repeatedly calls small functions AND profiling identifies meaningful invocation overhead, THEN flag calls for inlining.
Inline trivial functions: Replace suitable function calls with their equivalent operations.
Preserve correctness, evaluation order, and side effects; avoid excessive code duplication.
Fewer function calls, reduced execution overhead, and potentially lower energy consumption.
https://www.usenix.org/conference/java-vm-02/empirical-study-method-lining-java-just-time-compiler
C2.S3.R2
Excessive fragmentation of sequential operations
IF multiple lightweight functions are repeatedly executed sequentially AND their combined overhead is significant, THEN flag them for fusion.
Function fusion: Combine compatible lightweight operations into a single function or processing pass.
Preserve control flow, data dependencies, error handling, and maintainability.
Reduced call and intermediate-processing overhead, potentially improving runtime and energy efficiency.
