C12.S1.R1
Inefficient large-stride traversal
Nested loops traverse a contiguous row-major array along columns in the inner loop, producing large strides between successive accesses.
Reorder loop iteration to traverse contiguous elements first; use cache blocking or tiling for large matrices.
Preserve dependencies and output semantics; confirm array memory order (C versus Fortran).
Improved spatial locality and cache-line utilization; potentially fewer cache misses and lower execution time.
