C12.S2.R1
Scattered access to large arrays
Profiling shows frequent cache misses during repeated random or irregular accesses to a large array or data structure.
Improve data locality by sorting or grouping indices, processing data in blocks, or using a cache-friendly data structure.
Reordering must preserve required semantics; sorting or grouping has overhead and is unsuitable when access order is significant.
Better cache utilization and potentially reduced memory traffic and execution time.
[1], [3]
C12.S3.R1
Unpredictable branches in hot loops
Profiling or hardware counters show high branch-misprediction rates in a frequently executed, data-dependent conditional.
Consider branchless transformations, data partitioning, or separating predictable cases where these approaches are semantically equivalent.
Branchless code is not always faster; avoid unsafe arithmetic, excessive vector operations, and transformations that change behavior.
Fewer branch mispredictions and pipeline stalls; potential performance and energy improvements.
