C12.S4.R1
Poor data layout for frequently accessed fields
Profiling indicates that frequently used fields are interleaved with unused data, causing unnecessary cache-line loads in performance-critical loops.
Consider structure-of-arrays (SoA) instead of array-of-structures (AoS), or group frequently accessed fields together.
Depends on language, object layout, access patterns, and compiler/runtime behavior; validate with profiling.
Better spatial locality and fewer unnecessary memory transfers for suitable workloads.
